  + [forbidden_effect] is assignment
  + [forbidden_effect] is dispatch
  + [forbidden_effect] is operations_control
  + [forbidden_effect] is live_machine_control

  = must: make future proof trace evaluation fail or block if any forbidden effect is observed
  = must: keep future graph proof traces dry, bounded, and generated-output non-authoritative

& [P5GeneratedTraceNonpromotionRules] is the generated trace nonpromotion rule set
  + [rule] is generated runtime traces must live under future ignored generated trace roots when materialized
  + [rule] is generated runtime traces must cite fixture source, expected trace, operator node mapping, checkpoint basis, and proof ledger
  + [rule] is generated runtime traces must carry checkpoint nonauthority and generated-output nonpromotion notices
  + [rule] is generated runtime traces must not become SOP source authority, canonical specifications, proof ledgers, assignment records, dispatch records, operations records, or live-control records
  + [rule] is generated runtime traces may support completion review only through accepted proof ledger and accepted absence proof

  = must: reject generated trace promotion even when trace output matches the expected trace

& [P5S05DownstreamGate] is the gate opened by P5-S05
  + [opened_slice] is P5-S06 LangGraph adapter dependency deferral and implementation activation boundary
  + [activation_basis] is runtime proof trace fixture plan and no-live-effect execution boundary accepted
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_reason] is dependency posture and adapter activation decide when external LangGraph code may enter the project and when runtime implementation becomes safe
  + [completion_review_required] is true

  = must: open P5-S06 only after P5-S05 completion review accepts this proof trace fixture plan and no-live-effect execution boundary
